.TH CLAD 8 "2026-08-03" "0.8.0" "cli-assistant"
.SH NAME
clad \- Command Line Assistant daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clad
.SH DESCRIPTION
clad is the D-Bus daemon behind cli-assistant. It owns the
com.redhat.lightspeed.chat, com.redhat.lightspeed.history, and
com.redhat.lightspeed.user service names on the system bus, sends requests to
the configured OpenAI-compatible API, and stores history in SQLite.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The daemon reads configuration from /etc/cli-assistant/config.toml, with XDG
configuration paths and defaults as documented in the README.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Stop the daemon.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cli-assistant/config.toml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cli-assistant/cla.db
SQLite history database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR c (1)
